A42 — exec children directly, take the linker only when exec is refused

A40 routes every child through /system/bin/linker64 because the modern host
variant (targetSdk >= 29) may not exec a binary out of its own data directory.
The legacy variant may, and does for everything it starts itself. Under
gamescope it still got the linker route, and wine does not survive that
without help: its loader derives the library directory from /proc/self/exe,
which is the linker's path, so it dies at startup with

    wine: could not load ntdll.so: dlopen failed: library
    "/apex/com.android.runtime/bin/../lib/wine/aarch64-unix/ntdll.so" not found

The modern host hides this by redirecting /proc/self/exe for wine; the legacy
host has never needed to. Every gamescope session on a legacy build died this
way on a Retroid Pocket 6 (Proton 9 and Proton 10), while the same games on X11
on the same build ran.

Exec the child directly first, exactly as before A40, and go through the
linker only when the kernel answers EACCES. The modern variant's behaviour is
unchanged; the legacy variant gets its direct exec back.

diff --git a/src/Utils/Process.cpp b/src/Utils/Process.cpp
index cd133e7..67c42c7 100644
--- a/src/Utils/Process.cpp
+++ b/src/Utils/Process.cpp
@@ -99,6 +99,21 @@ static bool ResolveExecutablePath( const char *pszName, std::string &strOut )
 {
     static constexpr const char *kLinker = "/system/bin/linker64";
 
+    // The plain exec comes first. A host that may exec its own data directory
+    // (the legacy variant, targetSdk < 29) gets the child started the way it
+    // starts everything else, which matters for wine: started through the
+    // linker, its /proc/self/exe is the linker's and it looks for ntdll.so
+    // beside that ("/apex/com.android.runtime/bin/../lib/wine") unless the host
+    // redirects the path, which only the modern variant does. The linker route
+    // is taken only when the kernel refuses the exec, which is the modern
+    // variant's W^X denial.
+    execvp( argv[0], argv );
+    if ( errno != EACCES )
+    {
+        s_ProcessLog.errorf_errno( "Failed to start process \"%s\"", argv[0] ? argv[0] : "(null)" );
+        _exit( 0 );
+    }
+
     std::string strProgram;
     if ( argv[0] != nullptr
         && strcmp( argv[0], kLinker ) != 0
@@ -112,13 +127,9 @@ static bool ResolveExecutablePath( const char *pszName, std::string &strOut )
         linkerArgv.push_back( nullptr );
 
         execv( kLinker, linkerArgv.data() );
-        // Fall through: if the linker route is unavailable, try the plain exec
-        // so the failure reported is the real one.
     }
 
-    execvp( argv[0], argv );
-
-    s_ProcessLog.errorf_errno( "Failed to start process \"%s\"", argv[0] ? argv[0] : "(null)" );
+    s_ProcessLog.errorf_errno( "Failed to start process \"%s\" through %s", argv[0] ? argv[0] : "(null)", kLinker );
     _exit( 0 );
 }
 #else
